Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] LOCAL: ASoC: qcom: q6routing: accept S32_LE back ends

msm_routing_hw_params() records the bit width of S16_LE and S24_LE back
ends only. For an S32_LE back end bits_per_sample stays 0, so the ADM
device open asks the DSP for a 0-bit COPP and fails ("cmd = 0x10326
return error = 0x1"), and playback through it is impossible.

Record 32 bits for S32_LE. The Google Pixel 5 needs it for its speaker
amplifiers, which take full 32-bit TDM slots.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
index ea51120..30e57b9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
@@ -1170,6 +1170,9 @@ static int routing_hw_params(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE:
 			session->bits_per_sample = 24;
 		break;
+	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE:
+			session->bits_per_sample = 32;
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
